# GLAASGAMES — environment template.
#
# The REAL file lives at your Termux home, NOT in this repo:
#     /data/data/com.termux/files/home/.env      (i.e. $HOME/.env)
#
# Keeping it outside the working tree is deliberate. 00_GOVERNANCE/verify-no-secrets.ts
# scans every tracked file for credential patterns and fails the build on a hit, so a
# token committed here would break the gate — which is the gate working, not a nuisance.
# Copy this file to $HOME/.env, fill it in there, and leave this one as-is.
#
#     cp .env.example "$HOME/.env" && chmod 600 "$HOME/.env"
#
# scripts/termux-setup.sh reads $HOME/.env and generates .openclaude/settings.json.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Workers AI — the model backend OpenClaude talks to
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Cloudflare account ID. Dashboard -> Workers & Pages -> right sidebar,
# or `npx wrangler whoami`. A 32-character hex string. Not a secret, but the
# base URL is worthless without it.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# An API token with the "Workers AI" permission (Read is enough for inference).
# Create at: dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens -> Create Token
#   -> "Workers AI (Read)" template, or a custom token with Account / Workers AI / Read.
#
# THIS IS A SECRET. Never commit it, never paste it into a prompt, never echo it
# in a shell that logs. Use a scoped token, not a Global API Key — a Global Key
# authenticates every Cloudflare API on your whole account, including DNS and
# billing, and cannot be scoped down.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# The Workers AI model OpenClaude routes to.
#
# @cf/google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it is a Mixture-of-Experts model: 26B total
# parameters, ~4B active per forward pass, so it runs near 4B speed at closer to
# 26B quality. It advertises function calling, which an agent needs in order to
# use tools at all — a model without it cannot drive this repo.
#
# Override to try another catalog entry; the setup script does not validate the
# string beyond checking that the endpoint answers.
OPENCLAUDE_MODEL=@cf/google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres pair for `npm run verify:store`. Leave BOTH unset on Android: the
# store suite then reports its Postgres half as failed rather than silently
# passing (governance rule H8 — an unreachable database is not evidence). The
# SQLite half still runs and still proves the schema constraints.
# DATABASE_URL_ADMIN=
# DATABASE_URL_USER=
